{"status": "success", "data": {"classes": [{"strm": 2769, "crseId": 370925, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "RUSSL", "catalogNbr": "2158", "titleShort": "St. Petersburg & Modern Russia", "titleLong": "St. Petersburg and the Making of Modern Russia", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 18025, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:00AM", "timeEnd": "09:15AM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ol76", "firstName": "Olga", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Litvak"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/21/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "2158", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "SHUM", "catalogNbr": "2158", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "09/02/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Founded by Peter the Great in the early eighteenth century, St. Petersburg was built expressly to advertise the triumph of enlightened absolutism at home and to display Russia's status as a major European power abroad. But for all of its neo-classical splendor, the image of imperial St. Petersburg has been consistently invoked as a critical touchstone for the expression of political discontent, social unease and spiritual anxiety. The most modern and \"intentional\" of Russian cities, Russia's northern capital has come to stand for everything that's wrong with modern life. In this seminar, we will approach St. Petersburg as a cultural text composed by an illustrious trio of Russian writers who saw the complicated history of their country through Peter's \"window to the west\" -- Nikolai Gogol, Fyodor Dostoevsky and Andrei Bely.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS, HST-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 358416, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "RUSSL", "catalogNbr": "3331", "titleShort": "Intro To Russian Poetry", "titleLong": "Introduction to Russian Poetry", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 17128, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "04:55PM", "timeEnd": "06:10PM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "np27", "firstName": "Nancy", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Pollak"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/21/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "09/02/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "The nineteenth century was the first great age of Russian poetry \u2013 beginning with Pushkin's predecessors, continuing through Lermontov, and ending with Tiutchev and Fet and anticipations of modernism.\u00a0 In this course you'll learn how to read short poems carefully, you'll expand and deepen your understanding of the Russian language, and you'll gain insight into one of the world's major literary traditions.\u00a0 Reading in Russian, discussion in English.\u00a0 Satisfies the Russian Minor requirement for Russian literature with reading in the original.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS, ALC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "Reading in Russian; discussion in English.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: proficiency in Russian or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 353925, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "RUSSL", "catalogNbr": "3385", "titleShort": "Reading Nabokov", "titleLong": "Reading Nabokov", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 5955, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "03:00PM", "timeEnd": "04:15PM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "gs33", "firstName": "Gavriel", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Shapiro"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "In translation."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/21/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "COML", "catalogNbr": "3815", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "ENGL", "catalogNbr": "3790", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "09/02/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This course offers an exciting trip to the intricate world of Nabokov's fiction. After establishing himself in Europe as a distinguished Russian writer, Nabokov, at the outbreak of World War II, came to the United States where he reestablished himself, this time as an American writer of world renown. In our analysis of Nabokov's fictional universe, we shall focus on his Russian corpus of works, from Mary (1926) to The Enchanter (writ. 1939), all in English translation, and then shall examine the two widely read novels which he wrote in English in Ithaca while teaching literature at Cornell: Lolita (1955) and Pnin (1957).", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(LA-AS, ALC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "In translation.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 353928, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "RUSSL", "catalogNbr": "4492", "titleShort": "Superv Reading Russian Lit", "titleLong": "Supervised Reading in Russian Literature", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "601", "classNbr": 4518, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "vt13", "firstName": "Viktoria", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Tsimberov"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Independent Study. Prerequisite: students must find an advisor and submit a plan before signing up."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/21/2020", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "IS", "instrModeDescrshort": "Indp Stds", "instrModeDescr": "I